{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:cf3ea387158461f8","name":"Twin-228 Airspeeder","source":{"id":"source:reference-cf3ea387158461f8","title":"Twin-228 Airspeeder","revision":24781,"timestamp":"2024-11-06T19:11:08Z","sha256":"1fc55db66278b3dc7d7469d061fc7f8126e4d9df4fff0ad6f25ce18ccf125ded","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24781","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Twin-228%20Airspeeder&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-cf3ea387158461f8","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Iridonian Darkness"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Iridonian_Darkness"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Another design popularized by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The SoroSuub Corporation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_SoroSuub_Corporation","referenceId":"reference:98bcb386dd9e3201"},", the Twin-228 Airspeeder is a two-person speeder that shares aesthetic similarities with other contemporary ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," designs. The cockpit is situated toward the rear, with two sets of prongs stretching forward from the cockpit for over half of the Airspeeder's length. Two large engines at the rear of the Twin-228 give it a decent top speed, but like civilian ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"},", the Twin-228 never gets up to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," speeds.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One advantage of the Twin-228 has over other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," of the time is that its two-pronged front section is easily attached to cargo carriers, allowing it to haul moderate amounts of cargo in addition to providing simple transport. This increased cargo capacity comes at the expense of comfort for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and passenger, but must accept this as a necessary aspect of the Airspeeder's design. ",{"tag":"a","children":["The SoroSuub Corporation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_SoroSuub_Corporation","referenceId":"reference:98bcb386dd9e3201"}," sells a standard Cargo Pod designed specifically for use with the Twin-228, and it has proven to be one of the highest selling add-ons. As a result, the Twin-228 Airspeeder has also become popular among citizens of agricultural worlds, where the Airspeeders are used to carry equipment from one farm to another.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Twin-228 Airspeeder Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +9; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 16 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 16; +3 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehi